# ARK Operational Design Constitution

ARK operations surfaces should feel like one continuous shop workflow, not separate CRUD resources.

## Core Posture

- Default to read-first operational review.
- Treat edit/build modes as intentional, temporary mutation tools.
- Preserve service-lane continuity across customers, vehicles, repair orders, estimates, and documents.
- Prefer one worksheet with sectional rhythm over detached SaaS cards.
- Never make permanently editable surfaces the default posture.

## Density

- Increase density carefully, roughly 15% at a time.
- Preserve readability, line rhythm, and calm scanning.
- Avoid ERP compression, dashboard theater, and empty SaaS air.
- Tighten repeated headers, excessive padding, and stacked floating panels before adding new structure.

## Hierarchy

The eye should quickly identify:

- Vehicle identity.
- Customer identity.
- Repair order/workflow posture.
- Concern state.
- Estimate lines.
- Totals and financial authority.

Use hierarchy through typography, spacing, borders, and restrained state labels before adding color or widgets.

## Typography

- Operational labels should be small, uppercase, and useful.
- Customer and vehicle identity should be stronger than surrounding metadata.
- Concern headers should be compact and authoritative.
- Line descriptions should read before secondary metadata.
- Note lines should be visibly quieter but still intentional.
- Totals should use tabular numeric rhythm and stronger final-total weight.
- Avoid making all secondary text equally muted.

## Workflow State

- Color communicates operational state, not decoration.
- Approved work, active work, blocked work, and terminal work may use restrained semantic cues.
- Do not turn repair order status into workflow-engine UI.
- State language should feel human, subtle, and shop-operational.

## Forms And AJAX

- Forms appear on intent.
- AJAX should preserve workflow continuity, focus, and scroll where it meaningfully improves speed.
- AJAX must not move business authority into the client.
- Blade and Laravel remain the source of truth for workflow and financial decisions.

## Documents And PDFs

- Printed estimates are primary product surfaces.
- Customer-facing documents must feel professionally intentional.
- Keep PDF/document hierarchy aligned with live review posture.
- Do not let export templates drift into separate visual language.

## Financial Authority

- Totals must have one authoritative calculation path.
- UI may emphasize totals, but must not calculate financial truth.
- Estimate totals should act as visual center of gravity without overpowering the worksheet.

## Anti-Regression

Do not regress toward:

- Nova/Filament/admin-panel feeling.
- Generic resource CRUD pages.
- Floating card stacks.
- Airy SaaS spacing.
- Brittle SPA architecture.
- Workflow-engine ornamentation.
- Old-school ERP sludge.
